#SCRIPT
# ===========================================================================
#  IOQ automation
#  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Fields assigned below are filled in for you, so they are NOT asked as
#  questions when you generate a protocol:
#
#    * EFFECTIVEDATE          - stamped from today's date.
#    * QUALIFICATIONDECISION  - a drop-down (a "match" subject). Each choice
#      writes the matching final-status wording and release statement used in
#      the Final Summary section.
# ===========================================================================

# Auto-stamp the protocol effective date.
EFFECTIVEDATE = format(system.date, "yyyy-MM-dd")

# The overall decision drives the final status wording and release disposition.
match QUALIFICATIONDECISION:
    case "Qualified":
        FINALQUALIFICATIONSTATUS = "Qualified"
        RELEASESTATEMENT = "All IQ and OQ acceptance criteria were met. The equipment is released for routine use."
    case "Conditionally Qualified":
        FINALQUALIFICATIONSTATUS = "Conditionally Qualified"
        RELEASESTATEMENT = "Released under documented conditions; open items are tracked to closure through the deviation process."
    case "Not Qualified":
        FINALQUALIFICATIONSTATUS = "Not Qualified"
        RELEASESTATEMENT = "Acceptance criteria were not met. The equipment must not be used until deviations are resolved and the affected tests are repeated."
    case _:
        FINALQUALIFICATIONSTATUS = ""
        RELEASESTATEMENT = ""
#ENDSCRIPT
\begin{center}
\textbf{ INSTALLATION AND OPERATIONAL QUALIFICATION (IOQ) }

\textbf{ {EQUIPMENTNAME} ({ASSETID}) }

Document {DOCUMENTID}  |  Revision {REVISIONNO}  |  Effective {EFFECTIVEDATE}  |  Status: {DOCUMENTSTATUS}
\end{center}

This is an illustrative example. Tailor it to the equipment, approved user requirements, risk assessment, applicable regulations, manufacturer instructions, and site SOPs before execution.

\section{1. Document Control}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
\textbf{Equipment Name} & {EQUIPMENTNAME} & \textbf{Asset ID} & {ASSETID} \\
\textbf{Manufacturer} & {MANUFACTURER} & \textbf{Model} & {MODEL} \\
\textbf{Serial Number} & {SERIALNUMBER} & \textbf{Location} & {LOCATION} \\
\textbf{Department} & {DEPARTMENT} & \textbf{Site} & {SITENAME} \\
\textbf{Change Control No.} & {CHANGECONTROLNO} & \textbf{Validation Plan No.} & {VALIDATIONPLANNO} \\
\textbf{URS No.} & {URSNO} & \textbf{Risk Assessment No.} & {RISKASSESSMENTNO} \\
\textbf{Effective Date} & {EFFECTIVEDATE} & \textbf{Target Completion} & {TARGETCOMPLETIONDATE} \\
\end{tabular}

\subsection{Protocol Approval}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
\textbf{Role} & \textbf{Name} & \textbf{Signature} & \textbf{Date} \\
Prepared By & {PREPAREDBYNAME} & & {PREPAREDBYDATE} \\
Engineering & {ENGINEERINGNAME} & & {ENGINEERINGDATE} \\
Validation & {VALIDATIONNAME} & & {VALIDATIONDATE} \\
Quality Assurance & {QANAME} & & {QADATE} \\
\end{tabular}

\section{2. Purpose and Scope}

The purpose of this IOQ is to provide documented evidence that {EQUIPMENTNAME} ({ASSETID}) is installed in accordance with approved design, manufacturer, utility, safety, and documentation requirements, and that it operates consistently throughout its defined operating ranges and intended functions. Successful completion provides the documented basis for {NEXTQUALIFICATIONSTAGE}, subject to closure or formal acceptance of all deviations and open items.

Included scope: {INCLUDEDSCOPE}

Excluded scope: {EXCLUDEDSCOPE}

\section{3. Equipment Description}

\begin{tabular}{ll}
\textbf{Intended Use} & {INTENDEDUSE} \\
\textbf{Area Classification} & {AREACLASSIFICATION} \\
\textbf{Operating Principle} & {OPERATINGPRINCIPLE} \\
\textbf{Capacity / Range} & {CAPACITYORRANGE} \\
\textbf{Critical Parameters} & {CRITICALPARAMETERS} \\
\textbf{Control System} & {CONTROLSYSTEMDESCRIPTION} \\
\textbf{Software / Firmware} & {SOFTWAREFIRMWAREVERSION} \\
\textbf{Utilities Required} & {UTILITIESREQUIRED} \\
\end{tabular}

\section{4. Acceptance Criteria}

Each test step is marked Pass or Fail against its stated expected result. Objective evidence is attached or cross-referenced where required.

\begin{itemize}
\item All prerequisites are complete or formally approved to proceed.
\item Each IQ and OQ test meets its acceptance criteria, or any exception is documented and assessed through the approved deviation process.
\item Critical deviations are closed before final IOQ approval unless a documented quality decision permits a defined conditional status.
\end{itemize}

\begin{tabular}{ll}
\textbf{Overall Acceptance Rule} & {OVERALLACCEPTANCERULE} \\
\textbf{Retest Rule} & {RETESTRULE} \\
\end{tabular}

\section{5. Prerequisites}

\begin{tabular}{lll}
\textbf{No.} & \textbf{Prerequisite} & \textbf{Status} \\
1 & Approved IOQ protocol, URS, and risk assessment are available. & {PREREQ01STATUS} \\
2 & Installation / commissioning is complete to the required stage. & {PREREQ02STATUS} \\
3 & Required utilities are available and released for testing. & {PREREQ03STATUS} \\
4 & Measuring instruments are calibrated and within validity. & {PREREQ04STATUS} \\
5 & Personnel are trained and the area is released for execution. & {PREREQ05STATUS} \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
\textbf{Reviewed By} & {PREREQVERIFIEDBY} & \textbf{Date} & {PREREQREVIEWDATE} \\
\end{tabular}

\section{6. Installation Qualification (IQ)}

IQ verifies that {EQUIPMENTNAME} and its supporting components are installed and documented in accordance with approved requirements.

\subsection{IQ-1: Equipment Identification and Installation}

\begin{tabular}{ll}
\textbf{Objective} & Verify equipment identity, nameplate, and installed location against approved records. \\
\textbf{Acceptance} & Name, manufacturer, model, serial number, and asset ID all agree with approved documentation. \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{lllll}
\textbf{Step} & \textbf{Action / Challenge} & \textbf{Expected Result} & \textbf{Actual} & \textbf{P/F} \\
1 & Inspect nameplate and identification labels. & Legible; shows required identification and ratings. & {IQ1S1ACTUAL} & {IQ1S1PF} \\
2 & Compare manufacturer, model, and serial to records. & Match approved procurement / asset records. & {IQ1S2ACTUAL} & {IQ1S2PF} \\
3 & Verify asset tag and installed location. & Tag matches {ASSETID}; location matches {LOCATION}. & {IQ1S3ACTUAL} & {IQ1S3PF} \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
\textbf{Test Result} & {IQ1RESULT} & \textbf{Deviation No.} & {IQ1DEVIATION} \\
\textbf{Executed By} & {IQ1EXECBY} & \textbf{Date} & {IQ1EXECDATE} \\
\end{tabular}

\subsection{IQ-2: Utilities and Connections}

\begin{tabular}{ll}
\textbf{Objective} & Verify utilities and connections are installed to specification and safely terminated. \\
\textbf{Acceptance} & Electrical supply, grounding, and required utilities meet the approved specification. \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{lllll}
\textbf{Step} & \textbf{Action / Challenge} & \textbf{Expected Result} & \textbf{Actual} & \textbf{P/F} \\
1 & Verify electrical supply and grounding. & Supply and grounding match the approved specification. & {IQ2S1ACTUAL} & {IQ2S1PF} \\
2 & Verify utility connections against {UTILITIESREQUIRED}. & Required utilities are connected, labelled, and leak-free. & {IQ2S2ACTUAL} & {IQ2S2PF} \\
3 & Inspect for installation defects. & No unacceptable defects, loose fittings, or exposed wiring. & {IQ2S3ACTUAL} & {IQ2S3PF} \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
\textbf{Test Result} & {IQ2RESULT} & \textbf{Deviation No.} & {IQ2DEVIATION} \\
\textbf{Executed By} & {IQ2EXECBY} & \textbf{Date} & {IQ2EXECDATE} \\
\end{tabular}

\subsection{IQ-3: Documentation and Software Configuration}

\begin{tabular}{ll}
\textbf{Objective} & Verify required documents and the installed software / firmware baseline. \\
\textbf{Acceptance} & Required documents are available at approved status; software / firmware matches the approved version. \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{lllll}
\textbf{Step} & \textbf{Action / Challenge} & \textbf{Expected Result} & \textbf{Actual} & \textbf{P/F} \\
1 & Verify manuals, drawings, and certificates. & Required documents are available and current. & {IQ3S1ACTUAL} & {IQ3S1PF} \\
2 & Verify installed software / firmware version. & Matches approved version {SOFTWAREFIRMWAREVERSION}. & {IQ3S2ACTUAL} & {IQ3S2PF} \\
3 & Verify configuration baseline is recorded. & Configuration baseline is captured and controlled. & {IQ3S3ACTUAL} & {IQ3S3PF} \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
\textbf{Test Result} & {IQ3RESULT} & \textbf{Deviation No.} & {IQ3DEVIATION} \\
\textbf{Executed By} & {IQ3EXECBY} & \textbf{Date} & {IQ3EXECDATE} \\
\end{tabular}

\section{7. Operational Qualification (OQ)}

OQ verifies that {EQUIPMENTNAME} operates as intended throughout its specified operating ranges and challenge conditions.

\subsection{OQ-1: Power-Up and Operating Modes}

\begin{tabular}{ll}
\textbf{Objective} & Verify start-up, normal operation, and each defined operating mode. \\
\textbf{Acceptance} & Equipment powers up cleanly and each operating mode performs as specified. \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{lllll}
\textbf{Step} & \textbf{Action / Challenge} & \textbf{Expected Result} & \textbf{Actual} & \textbf{P/F} \\
1 & Power up and observe start-up sequence. & Start-up completes with no unexpected faults. & {OQ1S1ACTUAL} & {OQ1S1PF} \\
2 & Operate across the defined range {CAPACITYORRANGE}. & Values track set points within acceptance tolerance. & {OQ1S2ACTUAL} & {OQ1S2PF} \\
3 & Exercise each defined operating mode. & Each mode behaves as specified. & {OQ1S3ACTUAL} & {OQ1S3PF} \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
\textbf{Test Result} & {OQ1RESULT} & \textbf{Deviation No.} & {OQ1DEVIATION} \\
\textbf{Executed By} & {OQ1EXECBY} & \textbf{Date} & {OQ1EXECDATE} \\
\end{tabular}

\subsection{OQ-2: Alarms and Safety Interlocks}

\begin{tabular}{ll}
\textbf{Objective} & Verify alarms and safety interlocks trigger and respond correctly. \\
\textbf{Acceptance} & Each alarm and interlock activates at its set point and drives the correct safe response. \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{lllll}
\textbf{Step} & \textbf{Action / Challenge} & \textbf{Expected Result} & \textbf{Actual} & \textbf{P/F} \\
1 & Challenge high / low alarms. & Alarms annunciate within acceptance tolerance. & {OQ2S1ACTUAL} & {OQ2S1PF} \\
2 & Trigger each safety interlock. & Interlock drives the equipment to its defined safe state. & {OQ2S2ACTUAL} & {OQ2S2PF} \\
3 & Simulate a power interruption and restore. & Equipment restores to a safe, defined condition. & {OQ2S3ACTUAL} & {OQ2S3PF} \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
\textbf{Test Result} & {OQ2RESULT} & \textbf{Deviation No.} & {OQ2DEVIATION} \\
\textbf{Executed By} & {OQ2EXECBY} & \textbf{Date} & {OQ2EXECDATE} \\
\end{tabular}

\subsection{OQ-3: Security, Data and Backup / Restore}

\begin{tabular}{ll}
\textbf{Objective} & Verify user access control and, where applicable, data backup and restore. \\
\textbf{Acceptance} & Access levels enforce the security policy; backup and restore complete and verify successfully. \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{lllll}
\textbf{Step} & \textbf{Action / Challenge} & \textbf{Expected Result} & \textbf{Actual} & \textbf{P/F} \\
1 & Log in at operator and supervisor levels. & Access rights match the approved security policy. & {OQ3S1ACTUAL} & {OQ3S1PF} \\
2 & Perform a data backup. & Backup completes to the defined location and is recorded. & {OQ3S2ACTUAL} & {OQ3S2PF} \\
3 & Restore from backup and verify. & Restored data matches the source within acceptance criteria. & {OQ3S3ACTUAL} & {OQ3S3PF} \\
\end{tabular}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
\textbf{Test Result} & {OQ3RESULT} & \textbf{Deviation No.} & {OQ3DEVIATION} \\
\textbf{Executed By} & {OQ3EXECBY} & \textbf{Date} & {OQ3EXECDATE} \\
\end{tabular}

\section{8. Deviation Log}

\begin{tabular}{lllll}
\textbf{Deviation No.} & \textbf{Test Ref.} & \textbf{Description} & \textbf{Classification} & \textbf{Status} \\
{DEV01NO} & {DEV01TESTREF} & {DEV01DESC} & {DEV01CLASS} & {DEV01STATUS} \\
{DEV02NO} & {DEV02TESTREF} & {DEV02DESC} & {DEV02CLASS} & {DEV02STATUS} \\
{DEV03NO} & {DEV03TESTREF} & {DEV03DESC} & {DEV03CLASS} & {DEV03STATUS} \\
\end{tabular}

\section{9. Final Summary}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
\textbf{IQ Result} & {IQOVERALLRESULT} & \textbf{OQ Result} & {OQOVERALLRESULT} \\
\textbf{Total Deviations} & {TOTALDEVIATIONS} & \textbf{Open Deviations} & {OPENDEVIATIONS} \\
\end{tabular}

Residual risk assessment: {RESIDUALRISKASSESSMENT}

Based on execution and review of this protocol, {EQUIPMENTNAME} is determined to be \textbf{ {FINALQUALIFICATIONSTATUS}} for {RELEASESCOPE}. {RELEASESTATEMENT} The equipment may proceed to {NEXTQUALIFICATIONSTAGE}.

\begin{tabular}{ll}
\textbf{Released For} & {RELEASESCOPE} \\
\textbf{Requalification Due} & {REQUALIFICATIONDUEDATE} \\
\end{tabular}

\section{10. Final Approval and Release}

\begin{tabular}{llll}
\textbf{Role} & \textbf{Name} & \textbf{Signature} & \textbf{Date} \\
Equipment Owner & {FINALOWNERNAME} & & {FINALOWNERDATE} \\
Engineering & {FINALENGNAME} & & {FINALENGDATE} \\
Validation & {FINALVALNAME} & & {FINALVALDATE} \\
Quality Assurance & {FINALQANAME} & & {FINALQADATE} \\
\end{tabular}

\emph{Final qualification status: {FINALQUALIFICATIONSTATUS}. Protocol printed {= format(system.now, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm") }.}
